kosha link-length

  -- the physical length of a robot link (bone/rekha) in the kinematic chain
  -- this is the L in the IK formula: cos(θ2) = (x²+y²-L1²-L2²)/(2·L1·L2)
  -- and the L in moment of inertia: I = (1/3)·m·L²
  --
  -- 3D perspective: the bone's rest-length in local space
  -- physics perspective: the arm of the lever — determines torque sensitivity

